e  to discuss how we can clear the air move  things forward on a better footing and  that offer still stands  what does standing new ground look like  it looks like what we did um you know if  i  knew that again that low paid workers  were going to be pushed  into real punishing hardship i would  take a stand for them i would always  do that and i'm glad we did it because  it wasn't right was it  was it right to say that they were only  worth two-thirds of their wages  while other people are worth four fifths  now that's the bottom line isn't it  people  the government say that i was  showboating or i was political posturing  no i wasn't there was a point of  principle involved and i always act but  there's principle  involved it's like with the three  million excluded at the moment okay  there's a point of principle involved  there too  how can you give some people eighty  percent of their income  but leave three million people out in  the cold with absolutely nothing  that's the point of principle that's why  i'm taking a stand on that but it's also  why i took a stand  over over people's wages if it's pure  politics well people will make their own  judgments about that and then  they will rightly conclude that that is  showboating but i  act where there was a point of principle  that is what standing your ground  looks like i've learned to do that over  the years on the various issues that  i've worked on from hillsborough to a  whole range of other issues  you know i came to a point in politics  where i wasn't prepared to go along with  the  the ways of westminster anymore the way  they like to to do things  somebody needs to stand up to them and  whether where they affect the lives of  people in greater manchester  particularly the lowest paid  i will always stand my ground  finally with the respect mr mayor that  you know you  are looking after the people of greater  manchester the prime minister has got to  look after the united kingdom he's got  enough on his plate dealing with  the devolved nations without pesky  politicians  in the regions giving him grief as well  when he's trying to save as many lives  as possible  well that would be a fair criticism if  we hadn't offered  all year to him to help and i promise  you  it was all year what can we do involve  us more let us take more of the strain  with test and trace k  and i can't remember how many times i  came on your program  saying that that we were prepared to  take more responsibility for these  things to help him  and the government so they didn't listen  they didn't listen  all year and they kept centralizing uh  everything so  you know there's only so many times you  you can offer but but as i say  the office still stands you know i'm  somebody who cares about this country  cares about the people of this country i  always want to do the best buy them as  far as i  see it and going back to what i did in  october i  passionately believe that that was the  right stand to take and  actually it's led to better protection  now as people go back into  into tier three on thursday so i don't  regret it  if the government can't handle that well  punish me  but why punish every other local  authority in the country by just cutting  them out of the discussion  that doesn't sound to me like very  responsible grown-up government and i  think this government needs to  to kind of mature a little now in its  approach it's been in for a year  it takes a while for a government to  find its fee but i think they need to  find a better way of working with people  involve more people respect the role of  local  and regional government

